# This file exists solely to make scratch/ materialize in every clone and every git worktree.
#
# scratch/ is the canonical location for throwaway dev/agent scratch in this repo: probe scripts,
# run logs, one-off verification .m files -- anything you would otherwise be tempted to drop in
# tmp/ and delete before committing. Its CONTENTS are gitignored (see .gitignore's `scratch/*` +
# `!scratch/.gitkeep` pair), so nothing you put here can reach a commit and no cleanup step is
# needed before `git add -A`.
#
# Do not `rm -rf` this folder. There is no reason to: it is invisible to git, and when the
# worktree it lives in is removed after its PR merges, the scratch goes with it. A recursive rm
# bundled into the same shell call as a heredoc commit message is exactly what tripped a
# confirmation prompt for Seb on 2026-09-05 and prompted this convention.
#
# Keep durable output (code, results, caches, figures) OUT of here -- that belongs in the
# repository proper, tracked, or under localCache/ if it is large and regenerable.
